# Cloudflare Pages serves files; React Router owns paths.
#
# Without this, /garage works when reached by clicking a link - the router
# handles it in the browser and no request is made - and returns 404 when the
# same URL is typed, refreshed, or opened from a bookmark, because no file of
# that name exists. Every deep link in the application is affected, and none of
# it can be reproduced locally: `vite dev` answers index.html for unknown paths
# by default, so the bug appears for the first time in production.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser must keep the URL it asked for, so the router
# can read it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to / and lose it.
/*    /index.html   200